# DevOps

# Dockerfile Debugging

## Objective

Fix an existing Dockerfile without changing the base image or application data so that the image builds successfully.

---

## Initial Dockerfile Issues

The Dockerfile contained:

```dockerfile
COPY /server.crt ...
COPY /server.key ...
COPY ./index.html ...
```

Build failed with:

```text
failed to calculate checksum

"/index.html" not found
```

---

## Investigation

Checked the Docker build context:

```bash
cd /opt/docker

ls -l
```

Output:

```text
Dockerfile
certs/
html/
```

The actual files were located in:

```text
/opt/docker/certs/server.crt
/opt/docker/certs/server.key
/opt/docker/html/index.html
```

---

## Corrected COPY Statements

```dockerfile
COPY certs/server.crt /usr/local/apache2/conf/server.crt

COPY certs/server.key /usr/local/apache2/conf/server.key

COPY html/index.html /usr/local/apache2/htdocs/index.html
```

---

## Build Command

```bash
docker build -t httpd-image .
```

---

## Important Docker Concept Learned

Docker builds use a **build context**.

The build context was:

```text
/opt/docker
```

Docker can only access files inside this directory.

Incorrect:

```dockerfile
COPY /server.crt ...
```

Correct:

```dockerfile
COPY certs/server.crt ...
```

because the source path must be relative to the build context.

---

## Commands Used

```bash
cd /opt/docker

ls -l

vi Dockerfile

docker build -t httpd-image .
```

---

## Key Learning

Whenever Docker reports:

```text
COPY ... not found
```

the first troubleshooting step should be:

```bash
ls -R /opt/docker
```

to inspect the build context and ensure every `COPY` source path matches the actual directory structure.

